  "script": "Players who were called a waste of money, but proved everyone wrong. Real Madrid did something back then that a lot of people thought was insane, because they agreed to pay 45 million euros for a 16-year-old kid from Flamengo named Vinícius Júnior, who had played barely a handful of professional minutes. But the fee is not even the part that had scouts arguing for years. People were already calling him the new Neymar. And when Madrid unveiled him, the Brazilian legend Ronaldo walked him out and called him the biggest prospect in Brazilian football, while the club president said he could be one of the greatest of a whole new era. That is a mountain of pressure for a teenager, who cost the second highest fee in Brazilian history. But the higher they built him up, the harder his first few seasons fell apart. Vinícius was fast and thrilling to watch, yet his finishing let him down constantly. Because he would beat three defenders and then fluff the easy chance right in front of goal. Critics were roasting him, saying Madrid burned their money on a raw kid who couldn't score when it mattered. And then came the 2022 Champions League final in Paris, Real Madrid against Liverpool. In the 59th minute, Federico Valverde slid a low ball across the box and Vinícius crept in at the back post to tap home the only goal of the entire match. And the kid everyone had written off scored the goal that won Madrid a record fourteenth European Cup.",
